      "id": "external.v2.bundle_vectors",
      "title": "Normative V2 signed-bundle verification (bundle_vectors.json)",
      "claim": "Under default_verifier_policy with each case's committed verifier_policy_overrides, at 2026-10-22T00:00:00Z (inside the validity window of the base bundle and of every bundle expected to verify; some negatives are intentionally expired or not yet valid then), the signed bundle verifies, every committed mutation of it is rejected with its error_contains (the base is the control), the accepted bundles verify, the separately built rejected bundles are rejected with their error_contains, and the classical-only routine bundle gets its verdict per mode.",
      "limits": [
        "default_verifier_policy with each case's committed verifier_policy_overrides, plus the 4 modes for the classical-only bundle; no other policy is tried, although the vectors also claim every mode.",
        "must_reject_bundles are separately built bundles with no per-case control: each counts only if the base and the accepted bundles pass (a suite-level control, a weaker guarantee than a per-case control), and is judged on its committed error_contains.",
